<title>CHINA: China sets up phone lines for stock irregularities.</title>
<headline>China sets up phone lines for stock irregularities.</headline>
<dateline>SHANGHAI 1997-05-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>The China Securities Regulatory Commission (CSRC) has set up two special phone lines for investors to report irregularities and illegal trading on the stock markets, the Shanghai Securities News said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The CSRC, the securities watchdog, in a circular said the move was in line with Beijing's decision to make 1997 the year of risk control on the stock markets, the newspaper said.</p>
<p>The two numbers are (86-10) 6765-3134 and (86-10) 6765-3090, the newspaper said.</p>
</text>
